# NEXORA V0.2 — Real Market Data & API Layer

You are continuing development of the existing **NEXORA** project.

NEXORA is a premium Web3 On-Chain Intelligence Terminal.

Tagline:

> **Read the chain. Understand the flow.**

The project already has a completed V0.1 foundation with:

* Next.js 16 App Router
* TypeScript
* Tailwind CSS
* Dark terminal aesthetic
* Monospace financial numbers
* Restrained green/red colors
* Landing page `/`
* Dashboard `/dashboard`
* Markets `/markets`
* Dynamic token detail `/markets/[symbol]`
* Recharts charts
* Mock data architecture
* Coming Soon pages
* Responsive UI
* `npm run lint` passing
* `npm run build` passing

Your task is to implement **NEXORA V0.2 — Real Market Data & API Layer**.

---

# 1. IMPORTANT SCOPE

This phase is ONLY about replacing market-related mock data with real market data.

Do NOT implement:

* wallet connection
* MetaMask
* WalletConnect
* wagmi
* viem
* blockchain RPC
* smart contracts
* on-chain transaction indexing
* Smart Money
* portfolio wallet analysis
* real trading
* paper trading
* authentication
* AI
* database

Those belong to later phases.

Do not redesign the existing NEXORA UI unnecessarily.

Preserve the V0.1 visual identity and existing routes.

---

# 2. PRIMARY GOAL

Current architecture:

```text
Mock Data
    ↓
React Components
    ↓
NEXORA UI
```

Change it to:

```text
External Market API
        ↓
Next.js Server API
        ↓
Market Service
        ↓
Data Normalization
        ↓
NEXORA UI
```

The browser should NOT directly call CoinGecko.

Use Next.js server-side routes/services as the API boundary.

---

# 3. DATA PROVIDER

Use **CoinGecko API** for market data.

Prefer the current CoinGecko API structure/documentation available to the project.

Do not hardcode API keys into source code.

If the selected CoinGecko endpoint does not require an API key, allow the application to work without one.

If the selected endpoint requires an API key, use:

```env
COINGECKO_API_KEY=
```

Create:

```text
.env.example
```

Never commit real API keys.

Do not expose private API keys through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

---

# 4. API ARCHITECTURE

Create a clean service layer.

Suggested structure:

```text
src/
├── app/
│   └── api/
│       └── market/
│           ├── route.ts
│           └── [symbol]/
│               └── route.ts
│
├── lib/
│   ├── api/
│   │   └── market.ts
│   │
│   ├── mock-data/
│   │   ├── markets.ts
│   │   ├── charts.ts
│   │   └── activity.ts
│   │
│   ├── types.ts
│   │
│   └── utils/
│
└── components/
```

Adapt this structure to the existing project if equivalent files already exist.

Do NOT duplicate existing types or mock-data unnecessarily.

---

