# 35. API FAILURE TEST

Temporarily simulate API failure and verify that:

```text
API failure
    ↓
Error handled
    ↓
Fallback/demo state
    ↓
Application remains usable
```

Do not leave forced failure behavior in production.

---

# 36. BUILD QUALITY

Before finishing, inspect the existing project first.

Do not overwrite working V0.1 code unnecessarily.

Prefer incremental changes.

Do not duplicate:

* types
* components
* utilities
* API logic

Do not create unnecessary abstractions.

Use strict TypeScript.

Avoid `any`.

