# 37. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

V0.2 is complete when:

### Market data

* [ ] Dashboard uses real market data
* [ ] Markets page uses real market data
* [ ] Token detail uses real market data
* [ ] Prices are not hardcoded
* [ ] 24h changes are not hardcoded
* [ ] Market cap is not hardcoded
* [ ] Volume is not hardcoded

### API architecture

* [ ] External API is accessed server-side
* [ ] Market service exists
* [ ] Data is normalized
* [ ] UI does not depend on raw CoinGecko response
* [ ] API errors are handled
* [ ] 404 token handling exists

### Charts

* [ ] Historical chart uses real data
* [ ] 1D works
* [ ] 7D works
* [ ] 30D works
* [ ] Tooltip works
* [ ] Loading state works
* [ ] Error state works

### Reliability

* [ ] API caching/revalidation exists
* [ ] Rate limit is handled
* [ ] Fallback architecture exists
* [ ] Demo/fallback state is clearly indicated

### Security

* [ ] No secret API key in client code
* [ ] `.env.example` exists if needed
* [ ] No credentials committed

### UI

* [ ] Existing V0.1 design remains intact
* [ ] Responsive behavior remains intact
* [ ] Loading states are polished
* [ ] Error states are polished
* [ ] Data source indicator exists
* [ ] Last updated information exists where appropriate

### Quality

* [ ] `npm run lint` passes
* [ ] `npm run build` passes
* [ ] No TypeScript errors
* [ ] No unnecessary `any`
* [ ] No console errors in normal usage
* [ ] Vercel-compatible

